<title>CANADA: Canadian flight attendants okay strike.</title>
<headline>Canadian flight attendants okay strike.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The union representing 2,600 flight atttendants at Canadian Airlines Corp said on Thursday that its members voted 91 percent in favor of a strike mandate to support contract demands.</p>
<p>The Airline Division of the Canadian Union of Public Employees said in a statement the vote was inspired by management demands for concessions.</p>
<p>Their previous contract expired Dec 31, 1995.</p>
<p>Sheri Cameron, chairwoman of the union bargaining committee, said management was seeking to further reduce the number of flight attendants on aircraft and other concessions.</p>
<p>Cameron said she hoped the appointment of a commissioner by the federal government would lead to a fair settlement.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100</p>
</text>
